COMPILATION OF: E49B2

D: Disk Print
L: List Source Program

   NO ERROR(S) IN PASS 1

   NO ERROR(S) IN PASS 2

PL/I-80 V1.4 COMPILATION OF: E49B2

   1 a 0000 E49B2:
   2 a 0006   procedure options(main);
   3 a 0006   /* [E2E-49/P2] the member-vs-member compare with the operands
   4 a 0006      INVERTED (E49B1 reversed).  Under either accepted form this
   5 a 0006      object must equal E49B1 with the two member-cell relocations
   6 a 0006      swapped in their slots -- if instead B1 and B2 come out byte-
   7 a 0006      identical, the encoding does NOT follow the written side and
   8 a 0006      [C334]'s positional law breaks for member pairs. */
   9 c 0006   dcl
  10 c 0006     1 rec,
  11 c 0006       2 na char(3),
  12 c 0006       2 nb char(3),
  13 c 0006       2 s2 char(2);
  14 c 0006   dcl k fixed bin(15);
  15 c 0006   if rec.nb = rec.na then k = 1;
  16 c 001D   put list('K=', k);
  17 c 003F   stop;
  18 a 0042 end E49B2;

CODE SIZE = 0042
DATA AREA = 000C
FREE SYMS = 3888
END  COMPILATION
